# 必考词 Unit01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit01核心词汇

{{abbreviation}}{{/əˌbriːviˈeɪʃn}}{{n. 缩写；缩写词}}{{"Dr." is an abbreviation for "Doctor."}}
{{abide}}{{/əˈbaɪd}}{{v. 遵守；忍受}}{{You must abide by the rules of the club.}}
{{abolish}}{{/əˈbɒlɪʃ}}{{v. 废除；取消}}{{The government decided to abolish the outdated regulation.}}
{{abrupt}}{{/əˈbrʌpt}}{{adj. 突然的；唐突的}}{{The meeting came to an abrupt end.}}
{{absorb}}{{/əbˈzɔːb}}{{v. 吸收；吸引}}{{Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the atmosphere.}}
{{abstain}}{{/əbˈsteɪn}}{{v. 戒除；弃权}}{{He abstained from voting on the issue.}}
{{absurd}}{{/əbˈsɜːd}}{{adj. 荒谬的；可笑的}}{{It is absurd to believe that the earth is flat.}}
{{abundance}}{{/əˈbʌndəns}}{{n. 丰富；充裕}}{{The region has an abundance of natural resources.}}
{{abuse}}{{/əˈbjuːz}}{{v./n. 滥用；虐待}}{{The report revealed the abuse of power by some officials.}}
{{accelerate}}{{/əkˈseləreɪt}}{{v. 加速；促进}}{{The government aims to accelerate economic growth.}}
{{accessible}}{{/əkˈsesəbl}}{{adj. 可进入的；易理解的}}{{The building is accessible to wheelchair users.}}
{{accommodate}}{{/əˈkɒmədeɪt}}{{v. 容纳；提供住宿}}{{The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests.}}
{{accomplish}}{{/əˈkʌmplɪʃ}}{{v. 完成；实现}}{{He accomplished his goal of running a marathon.}}
{{accumulate}}{{/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt}}{{v. 积累；积聚}}{{Dust had accumulated on the shelves over the months.}}
{{accurate}}{{/ˈækjərət}}{{adj. 准确的；精确的}}{{The report provides an accurate description of the situation.}}
{{accustom}}{{/əˈkʌstəm}}{{v. 使习惯}}{{It took her a while to accustom herself to the new environment.}}
{{achieve}}{{/əˈtʃiːv}}{{v. 达到；取得}}{{She achieved great success in her scientific research.}}
{{acknowledge}}{{/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ}}{{v. 承认；致谢}}{{He acknowledged his mistake and apologized publicly.}}
{{acquaint}}{{/əˈkweɪnt}}{{v. 使熟悉；使了解}}{{Let me acquaint you with the facts of the case.}}
{{acquire}}{{/əˈkwaɪər}}{{v. 获得；学到}}{{She acquired a new skill through online courses.}}
{{activate}}{{/ˈæktɪveɪt}}{{v. 激活；使活动}}{{The alarm was activated by the smoke.}}
{{acute}}{{/əˈkjuːt}}{{adj. 急性的；敏锐的；严重的}}{{The patient has acute appendicitis.}}
{{adapt}}{{/əˈdæpt}}{{v. 适应；改编}}{{It is important to adapt to changing circumstances.}}
{{adequate}}{{/ˈædɪkwət}}{{adj. 足够的；适当的}}{{The supply of food is adequate for the refugees.}}
{{adhere}}{{/ədˈhɪər}}{{v. 粘附；坚持；遵守}}{{You must adhere to the safety regulations.}}
{{adjacent}}{{/əˈdʒeɪsnt}}{{adj. 邻近的；毗连的}}{{The hotel is adjacent to the beach.}}
{{adjust}}{{/əˈdʒʌst}}{{v. 调整；适应}}{{You need to adjust the mirror before driving.}}
{{administer}}{{/ədˈmɪnɪstər}}{{v. 管理；执行；给予}}{{The nurse administered the medicine to the patient.}}
{{adolescent}}{{/ˌædəˈlesnt}}{{n./adj. 青少年；青春期的}}{{Adolescent health is an important public health issue.}}
{{adopt}}{{/əˈdɒpt}}{{v. 采用；收养}}{{The company decided to adopt a new strategy.}}
{{adverse}}{{/ˈædvɜːs}}{{adj. 不利的；有害的}}{{The drug has adverse side effects.}}
{{advocate}}{{/ˈædvəkeɪt}}{{v./n. 提倡；倡导者}}{{Many scientists advocate for renewable energy sources.}}
{{affiliate}}{{/əˈfɪlieɪt}}{{v./n. 使附属；附属机构}}{{The hospital is affiliated with the university.}}
{{affirm}}{{/əˈfɜːm}}{{v. 断言；肯定；确认}}{{The witness affirmed that the statement was true.}}
{{affluent}}{{/ˈæfluənt}}{{adj. 富裕的；丰富的}}{{The affluent neighborhood has many luxury homes.}}
{{aggravate}}{{/ˈæɡrəveɪt}}{{v. 加重；使恶化}}{{The bad weather aggravated his illness.}}
{{aggregate}}{{/ˈæɡrɪɡeɪt}}{{v./n. 聚集；合计；总数}}{{The aggregate score of the two games was 5-3.}}
{{aggressive}}{{/əˈɡresɪv}}{{adj. 侵略性的；有进取心的}}{{The company adopted an aggressive marketing strategy.}}
{{agitate}}{{/ˈædʒɪteɪt}}{{v. 煽动；使焦虑；搅拌}}{{The news agitated the public.}}
{{alert}}{{/əˈlɜːt}}{{adj./v./n. 警觉的；提醒}}{{The government issued an alert about the approaching typhoon.}}
{{alienate}}{{/ˈeɪliəneɪt}}{{v. 使疏远；离间}}{{His behavior alienated his friends.}}
{{allege}}{{/əˈledʒ}}{{v. 宣称；指控；断言}}{{He is alleged to have committed the crime.}}
{{alleviate}}{{/əˈliːvieɪt}}{{v. 减轻；缓解}}{{The medicine helped alleviate the pain.}}
{{allocate}}{{/ˈæləkeɪt}}{{v. 分配；拨出}}{{The government allocated funds for education.}}
{{alternate}}{{/ˈɔːltəneɪt}}{{v./adj. 交替；轮流的；备选的}}{{We alternate between working from home and the office.}}
{{alternative}}{{/ɔːlˈtɜːnətɪv}}{{n./adj. 替代品；可选择的}}{{We need to find an alternative solution to this problem.}}
{{ambiguous}}{{/æmˈbɪɡjuəs}}{{adj. 模棱两可的；含糊的}}{{The instructions were ambiguous and confusing.}}
{{amend}}{{/əˈmend}}{{v. 修改；改善}}{{The law was amended to include new provisions.}}
{{analogy}}{{/əˈnælədʒi}}{{n. 类比；类推}}{{He drew an analogy between the brain and a computer.}}
{{anchor}}{{/ˈæŋkər}}{{n./v. 锚；使固定；主持}}{{The ship dropped anchor in the harbor.}}
{{annual}}{{/ˈænjuəl}}{{adj. 年度的；每年的}}{{The annual report shows significant growth in revenue.}}
{{anonymous}}{{/əˈnɒnɪməs}}{{adj. 匿名的；无名的}}{{The donation was made by an anonymous donor.}}
{{anticipate}}{{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt}}{{v. 预期；期望}}{{We anticipate a significant increase in demand.}}
{{apparatus}}{{/ˌæpəˈreɪtəs}}{{n. 器械；设备；机构}}{{The laboratory has modern scientific apparatus.}}
{{apparent}}{{/əˈpærənt}}{{adj. 明显的；表面上的}}{{It was apparent that she was not telling the truth.}}
{{appeal}}{{/əˈpiːl}}{{v./n. 呼吁；上诉；吸引力}}{{The charity made an appeal for donations.}}
{{appliance}}{{/əˈplaɪəns}}{{n. 器具；家用电器}}{{The kitchen is equipped with modern appliances.}}
{{applicable}}{{/əˈplɪkəbl}}{{adj. 适用的；可应用的}}{{The rule is applicable to all employees.}}
{{appoint}}{{/əˈpɔɪnt}}{{v. 任命；指定}}{{He was appointed as the new department manager.}}
{{appraise}}{{/əˈpreɪz}}{{v. 评估；鉴定}}{{Experts appraised the value of the painting.}}
{{appreciate}}{{/əˈpriːʃieɪt}}{{v. 感激；欣赏}}{{I really appreciate your help with this project.}}
{{apprehend}}{{/ˌæprɪˈhend}}{{v. 逮捕；理解；忧虑}}{{The police apprehended the suspect.}}
{{approach}}{{/əˈprəʊtʃ}}{{v./n. 接近；方法}}{{We need to approach this problem from a different perspective.}}
{{appropriate}}{{/əˈprəʊpriət}}{{adj. 适当的；合适的}}{{Please wear appropriate clothing for the interview.}}
{{approve}}{{/əˈpruːv}}{{v. 批准；赞成}}{{The board approved the new budget plan.}}
{{apt}}{{/æpt}}{{adj. 恰当的；易于…的；聪明的}}{{She is apt to forget things when she is busy.}}
{{arbitrary}}{{/ˈɑːbɪtrəri}}{{adj. 任意的；武断的}}{{The decision seemed arbitrary and unfair.}}
{{arise}}{{/əˈraɪz}}{{v. 出现；产生}}{{New challenges may arise during the project.}}
{{array}}{{/əˈreɪ}}{{n./v. 排列；一系列；部署}}{{The store has a wide array of products.}}
{{articulate}}{{/ɑːˈtɪkjuleɪt}}{{adj./v. 善于表达的；清楚表达}}{{She is very articulate and persuasive in debates.}}
{{ascend}}{{/əˈsend}}{{v. 上升；攀登}}{{They ascended the mountain slowly.}}
{{ascertain}}{{/ˌæsəˈteɪn}}{{v. 查明；确定}}{{The police are trying to ascertain the cause of the fire.}}
{{ascribe}}{{/əˈskraɪb}}{{v. 归因于；归咎于}}{{He ascribed his success to hard work.}}
{{aspire}}{{/əˈspaɪər}}{{v. 渴望；追求；有志于}}{{She aspires to become a doctor.}}
{{assemble}}{{/əˈsembl}}{{v. 集合；组装}}{{The students assembled in the auditorium for the lecture.}}
{{assert}}{{/əˈsɜːt}}{{v. 断言；主张；维护}}{{She asserted her right to speak at the meeting.}}
{{assess}}{{/əˈses}}{{v. 评估；评价}}{{Teachers assess students' progress through regular tests.}}
{{asset}}{{/ˈæset}}{{n. 资产；有价值的人或物}}{{Her experience is a valuable asset to the company.}}
{{assign}}{{/əˈsaɪn}}{{v. 分配；指定}}{{The teacher assigned homework to the students.}}
{{assimilate}}{{/əˈsɪmɪleɪt}}{{v. 同化；吸收；消化}}{{Immigrants often assimilate into the local culture.}}
{{assist}}{{/əˈsɪst}}{{v. 帮助；协助}}{{The nurse assisted the doctor during the operation.}}
{{associate}}{{/əˈsəʊʃieɪt}}{{v./n. 联系；同事}}{{People often associate the color red with passion.}}
{{assume}}{{/əˈsjuːm}}{{v. 假设；承担}}{{Let's assume that the project will be completed on time.}}
{{assure}}{{/əˈʃʊər}}{{v. 保证；使确信}}{{I assure you that the product is of high quality.}}
{{attach}}{{/əˈtætʃ}}{{v. 附上；重视}}{{Please attach your resume to the email.}}
{{attain}}{{/əˈteɪn}}{{v. 达到；获得}}{{She attained the highest score in the class.}}
{{attempt}}{{/əˈtempt}}{{v./n. 尝试；企图}}{{He attempted to climb the mountain but failed.}}
{{attend}}{{/əˈtend}}{{v. 出席；照料}}{{All students are expected to attend the lecture.}}
{{attribute}}{{/əˈtrɪbjuːt}}{{v./n. 归因于；属性}}{{She attributed her success to hard work.}}
{{audit}}{{/ˈɔːdɪt}}{{v./n. 审计；旁听}}{{The company's accounts are audited annually.}}
{{augment}}{{/ɔːɡˈment}}{{v. 增加；扩大；增强}}{{The company augmented its workforce to meet demand.}}
{{authentic}}{{/ɔːˈθentɪk}}{{adj. 真正的；真实的}}{{The restaurant serves authentic Italian food.}}
{{authorize}}{{/ˈɔːθəraɪz}}{{v. 授权；批准}}{{The manager authorized the purchase of new equipment.}}
{{automate}}{{/ˈɔːtəmeɪt}}{{v. 使自动化}}{{The factory automated its production line.}}
{{autonomy}}{{/ɔːˈtɒnəmi}}{{n. 自治；自主权}}{{The university has a high degree of academic autonomy.}}
{{avail}}{{/əˈveɪl}}{{v./n. 有用；效用；帮助}}{{All their efforts availed them nothing.}}
{{available}}{{/əˈveɪləbl}}{{adj. 可用的；有空的}}{{The manager is not available at the moment.}}
{{avert}}{{/əˈvɜːt}}{{v. 避免；转移}}{{Quick action averted a major disaster.}}
{{avid}}{{/ˈævɪd}}{{adj. 热衷的；渴望的}}{{She is an avid reader of science fiction.}}
{{avoid}}{{/əˈvɔɪd}}{{v. 避免；避开}}{{You should avoid eating too much sugar.}}
{{aware}}{{/əˈweər}}{{adj. 意识到的；知道的}}{{Are you aware of the risks involved in this project?}}
{{awkward}}{{/ˈɔːkwəd}}{{adj. 尴尬的；笨拙的}}{{There was an awkward silence after his comment.}}
